2026-08-16T13:14:02Z    [HD:Net sales] GATE critic: The 4.86% YoY rate you applied is inconsistent with Home Depot’s reported prior-year Q2. If FY2025 Q2 net sales were $45,300m, a 4.86% increase implies FY2024 Q2 of about $43,230m (45,300 / 1.0486). But HD’s reported FY2024 Q2 net sales were approximately $43,800m, which implies YoY growth of roughly 3.4%, not 4.86%. Using the overstated 4.86% inflates the FY2026 Q2 forecast by roughly $600–700m.
2026-08-16T13:14:08Z    [DE:Diluted EPS (GAAP)] GATE critic: Wrong fiscal period used as the anchor: you compounded FY2024Q3 diluted GAAP EPS of $6.29 forward two years to estimate FY2026Q3, but the proper like-for-like comparable is FY2025Q3 (the immediately preceding year’s Q3). Deere’s FY2025 Q3 diluted GAAP EPS was reported in its Aug 2025 8‑K/10‑Q, so anchoring to FY2024Q3 misaligns the period by one year and yields a misbased estimate.
