2026-08-16T13:14:31Z    [HD:Adjusted diluted EPS] GATE critic: Internal arithmetic inconsistency: Using your stated method—prior-year FY2025Q2 adjusted diluted EPS of $4.68 multiplied by (1 + 0.05%)—yields 4.68 × 1.0005 = 4.68234 (≈4.6823), not the proposed 4.68251 (nor 4.683). Either the applied growth rate or the rounding/calculation is off.
2026-08-16T13:14:40Z    [DE:Production & Precision Ag operating profit] GATE critic: The -12.65% YoY change you apply is built partly from FY2020Q3→FY2021Q3 (+49.8%, weight 0.37), which is not a like‑for‑like comparator for Production & Precision Ag: Deere adopted the current P&PA segment reporting in 2021 and FY2020Q3 was COVID‑depressed, making FY2021Q3 an exceptional rebound. Using that +49.8% as an input biases the FY2026Q3 estimate upward off the $580m FY2025Q3 base, so the figure rests on the wrong basis.
