2026-08-16T13:14:43Z    [HAS:Net fees] GATE critic: The -1.25% “post-guidance signal” (the -0.0125 tilt) you applied to FY2026 is sourced from commentary about FY2025’s near-term trading (a Q3 decline feeding into Q4 and “near‑term” conditions). Those effects pertain to FY2025 and are already reflected in the reported FY2025 net fees of £972.4m; applying them again to cut the FY2026 projection from 849.1 to 838.49 is a wrong-period adjustment that double-counts the weakness, biasing FY2026 too low.
2026-08-16T13:14:45Z    [ADI:Revenue] GATE critic: Your own arithmetic doesn’t match the stated blend: 3900 × 0.967 + 3112.9 × 0.033 = 3,874.0257 USDm, not 3,873.91. The proposed figure is internally inconsistent with its inputs and weights.
