2026-08-16T13:15:16Z    [HAS:Pre-exceptional basic EPS] GATE critic: You computed EPS from “operating profit 44.89 – net finance 13.4” with a single tax rate, but never adjust for exceptionals. That gives a statutory EPS, not the required pre-exceptional metric. This matters here: Hays discloses FY2025 pre-exceptional basic EPS of 4.03p versus statutory 1.31p (a ~3x gap), so using unadjusted operating profit will materially understate FY2026 pre-exceptional EPS. The proposed 1.285p is effectively on the statutory basis, not pre-exceptional.
2026-08-16T13:15:20Z    [ADI:Adjusted gross margin] GATE critic: The 71.95% baseline is built from the wrong periods and columns: the four inputs you averaged (69.9, 71.6, 74.1, 72.2) are a mix of “current” and “prior-year” Q3 figures from FY2020–FY2023 (e.g., FY2020Q3 current 71.6% vs prior-year 69.9%; FY2022Q3 current 72.2% vs prior-year 74.1%). That is neither the last four reported quarters nor a consistent set of current-period values for a single basis, so the FY2026Q3 forecast rests on an invalid, mis-timed baseline.
